Source: grimoire
Section: text
Priority: optional
Maintainer: mplx <jennifer@mplx.dev>
Homepage: https://grimoire.jennifer-lang.dev/
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/jennifer-language/grimoire
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/jennifer-language/grimoire.git
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: grimoire
Architecture: all
Depends: jennifer (>= @ENGINE_FLOOR@)
Recommends: git
Description: documentation website and printable PDF from Markdown files
 Grimoire builds a book - a directory of Markdown chapters and a
 grimoire.toml - into a static website with search, navigation, themes
 and a dark mode, and optionally into a printable PDF of the same book.
 The site works served from a web root, from a subdirectory, or opened
 straight off the disk.
 .
 The package is architecture-independent Jennifer source: the launcher at
 /usr/bin/grimoire is a symlink into /usr/share/grimoire, where bin/, src/
 and the shipped plugins sit side by side, because the launcher finds its
 modules relative to its own resolved path.
 .
 The versioned dependency on jennifer mirrors the [engines] table in
 Grimoire's deck.toml; the interpreter enforces the same floor at load time
 from each source file's `# pragma-jennifer-version:` header.
 .
 git is recommended, not required: it stamps the PDF footer with the
 book's version, and the feed and lastmod plugins date chapters from the
 git history. Without it those are left out, and the book still builds.
